{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Therefore pride is their necklace</b> — from the same root as וענקים לגרגרותיך (necklaces for your throat; Proverbs 1:9), like the form of a crown of gold, and יעטוף from the same root as המעטפות (wraps; Ezekiel 13:18)." "<b>violence</b> — like שית זונה (the fee of a prostitute; Deuteronomy 23:19), like דרך (way)." "And some say: כי יעטוף — like תפלה לעני כי יעטוף (a prayer when one is faint; Psalm 102:1)." "And the meaning of שית is פאה (corner/side). And the sense: that violence covers them on every side, as though it were in their domain."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 73, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:10.162180025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}